# =============================================================================
# Volare
#
# Rule: Git stores what a human wrote. It does not store what a tool can
# regenerate. If you are about to add an exception for a large binary, read
# docs/data-management.md first.
# =============================================================================

# --- Editor and OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*~
*.swp

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- MATLAB ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor autosaves and Simulink build scratch. The .slx models themselves are
# source and stay tracked.
*.asv
*.m~
*.autosave
slprj/
sccprj/
codegen/
*.slxc
*.mexa64
*.mexw64
*.mexmaci64

# --- Blender -----------------------------------------------------------------
# .blend1 (and .blend2) are Blender's automatic previous-version backups. They
# are byte-for-byte redundant with the .blend beside them and cost ~11 MB.
*.blend1
*.blend2
*.blend@

# --- FreeCAD -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.FCBak
*.FCStd1

# --- Build and run logs ------------------------------------------------------
*_build.log
powertrain_step_build.log

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit telemetry endpoints, API keys or radio credentials.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored ------------------------------------------------
# powertrain/output/ and cad/out/ hold generated artefacts that ARE tracked,
# because teammates without MATLAB or Blender still need them. That means a
# rerun shows them as modified. Commit a regenerated artefact only when the
# input actually changed; otherwise `git checkout -- <path>` to discard it.
